            <div xml:id="d572">

                <pb facs="0692" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00 Revolutions/95: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lay</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-15T18:00:00-04:00">May 15, 1931—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>41. Your 95, May 14, noon. The Department perceives no objection to the
                    publication by the Government of Honduras of the substance of its 40, May 13, 3
                    p.m. It is believed however that it would be desirable for you to examine the
                    text of the proposed statement prior to its publication.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
